description:
In edhoc.rs test std_convenience_constructors_remain_available at ~line 1847, the EdhocInitiator::new call still uses 2-arg .unwrap() form:

  let _ = EdhocInitiator::new([1; 32], 0).unwrap();

But EdhocInitiator::new now takes 3 args (seed, c_i, rng) and returns Self (not Result). This test only compiles if there is still a cfg(feature=std) fallback, otherwise it breaks. The std_convenience_constructors test name is also misleading since constructors no longer require std.
